  "generated_text": "1. **Calculate the distance Joann traveled:**\n   Joann rode her bike at an average speed of 12 miles per hour for 3.5 hours. To find the distance she traveled, we use the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given values, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 12 \\times 3.5 = 42 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the average speed Fran needs to ride:**\n   Fran rides for 3 hours and needs to travel the same distance of 42 miles. To find the average speed Fran needs to ride, we use the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given values, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed} = \\frac{42}{3} = 14 \\text{ miles per hour}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   Fran needs to ride her bike at $\\boxed{14}$ miles per hour.",
